    "status": "stub",
    "notes": "Not from an official source, which is the point: these are widely used but locally variable, so the UI always pairs them with the local-guidance note. Stays status=stub for that reason. Entries duplicated by the AFPC list were dropped so it wins. On 2026-09-15 the list was pruned against the AFPC acronyms page (re-fetched that day; it is a single table of 148 entries with no categories, all carried in hq-approved.json) and against what a reader anywhere in the Air Force recognises without expansion: what remains is grades and ranks, unit echelons (Sq, Grp, Wg, NAF, MAJCOM, HQ), the major commands and components, squadron and group types, duty positions, decorations, unit awards and ribbons, correspondence types, the fiscal calendar, and units of measure and magnitude. Removed: the Headquarters Air Force directorates A1-A9, whose phrases (Operations, Intelligence, Communications) are ordinary words; the officer pay grades O-1 to O-6, replaced by the rank abbreviations 2d Lt to Col that evaluations actually use; aircraft and weapon names mapped to designators (Eagle, Raptor, Reaper, Globemaster III, Sidewinder and the rest), which are not abbreviations and rewrote ordinary words; Dec and Mo, which collide with the month; the radio bands UHF, VHF, HF and LOS, JDAM and C3, which are field-specific; and DCSA, DISA, FBI, SOCOM and POAM, which are not Air Force common. A trailing parenthetical was treated as an annotation and stripped, except where stripping would collide: ASOR-L and ASOR-S keep '(Long)' and '(Short)'. Case-variant abbreviations (Qtr/qtr, QTRLY/QTR) are all kept so recognition matches whichever a writer used; replacement picks one deterministically."
  },
